# Staged by fisher-5sg.9 on 2026-11-25. See README.md for derivation.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# (go, info, bestmove and quit), and the owner's 2026-11-25 D17 answers
# on fisher-5sg.10, recorded as fisher-r6y D49–D52 and D56.
> position startpos
> go wtime 0
# D51 floors the clock at zero. The search may use 0 ms after the margin
# (D50). D20 gives no info and UCI bestmove requires one move.
< bestmove {legal}

> go wtime -500
# D51 floors the clock at zero. The search may use 0 ms after the margin
# (D50). D20 gives no info and UCI bestmove requires one move.
< bestmove {legal}

> go wtime 0 btime 60000
# D50 uses White's clock. D51 and D20 give 0 ms of usable time and
# no info. UCI bestmove requires one move for the accepted go.
< bestmove {legal}

> go wtime -500 btime 60000
# D50 uses White's clock. D51 and D20 give 0 ms of usable time and
# no info. UCI bestmove requires one move for the accepted go.
< bestmove {legal}

# UCI quit and D25 require clean exit with no further output.
> quit
! exit
